  "transcript": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "speaker": "agent",
      "kind": "opening",
      "text": "These questions are about the trial \"Stereotactic Magnetic Resonance Guided Radiation Therapy\". Your earlier answers already covered 2 of its rules. I'll ask about the rest of its rules one at a time. You can skip any question, and \"I don't know\" is always fine."
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "speaker": "agent",
      "kind": "question",
      "text": "Thanks. Have you been diagnosed with cancer that requires stereotactic body radiation therapy?",
      "criterionId": "P1"
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "speaker": "participant",
      "kind": "reply",
      "text": "Yes, I have non-small cell lung cancer. It's spread to my liver and my back bones."
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "speaker": "agent",
      "kind": "question",
      "text": "Thanks. Do you know the size of the tumor in your liver or back, specifically if it is 7 centimeters or smaller?",
      "criterionId": "P2"
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "speaker": "participant",
      "kind": "reply",
      "text": "You'd have to ask my doctor, dear. I'm a little vague on the exact measurements from the scans."
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "speaker": "agent",
      "kind": "question",
      "text": "Thanks. Are you 18 years of age or older?",
      "criterionId": "P3"
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "speaker": "participant",
      "kind": "reply",
      "text": "Yes, I'm 77 years old."
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "speaker": "agent",
      "kind": "question",
      "text": "Thanks. Are you willing and able to sign a written informed consent document for this study?",
      "criterionId": "P5"
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "speaker": "participant",
      "kind": "reply",
      "text": "Yes, I can sign that. I want to do everything I can to help."
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "speaker": "agent",
      "kind": "question",
      "text": "Thanks. Have you ever had an allergic reaction to gadolinium-based IV contrast (the dye used in some MRI scans)?",
      "criterionId": "P8"
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "speaker": "participant",
      "kind": "reply",
      "text": "No, I don't think so. I've never had a reaction to MRI dye."
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "speaker": "agent",
      "kind": "question",
      "text": "Thanks. To be sure, have you ever had any reaction (like hives, itching, or trouble breathing) after receiving the contrast dye for an MRI scan?",
      "criterionId": "P8"
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "speaker": "participant",
      "kind": "reply",
      "text": "No, I've never had any reaction like that to the dye for an MRI scan."
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "speaker": "agent",
      "kind": "question",
      "text": "Thanks. Do you have severe claustrophobia (fear of enclosed spaces) or anxiety that might make it difficult for you to stay still inside the MRI machine?",
      "criterionId": "P10"
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "speaker": "participant",
      "kind": "reply",
      "text": "I get a little anxious in tight spaces, but I can manage with some help. I don't have severe claustrophobia that would stop me."
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "speaker": "agent",
      "kind": "closing",
      "text": "Thank you, that's all my questions. Your record for this trial is ready, for you and your oncologist. They and the trial team decide whether it is right for you."
    }
  ],
